commentary:
Section 13 prescribes the statutory classification of income under the Act. Subject to other express provisions ("Save as otherwise provided in this Act"), all incomes must be categorized under five designated heads for the dual purposes of the charge of income-tax and the computation of total income. These heads are:
(a) Salaries;
(b) Income from house property;
(c) Profits and gains of business or profession;
(d) Capital gains; and
(e) Income from other sources.

By categorizing receipts into these five heads, the section sets the foundational framework for computing total income and levying the charge of income-tax across the Act.

Interpretation: The opening clause "Save as otherwise provided in this Act" indicates that while classification under these five heads is the general rule, any specific statutory exceptions or alternative computation provisions established elsewhere in the Act will prevail over this general requirement.
